<article class="env-remark" id="03QM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03QM">Remark <span data-tag="03QM">59.33.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $s \in S$. If $S$ is locally Noetherian then $\mathcal{O}_{S, s}^ h$ is also Noetherian and it has the same completion: </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \widehat{\mathcal{O}_{S, s}} \cong \widehat{\mathcal{O}_{S, s}^ h}.  \]
</div>
  <p> In particular, $\mathcal{O}_{S, s} \subset \mathcal{O}_{S, s}^ h \subset \widehat{\mathcal{O}_{S, s}}$. The henselization of $\mathcal{O}_{S, s}$ is in general much smaller than its completion and inherits many of its properties. For example, if $\mathcal{O}_{S, s}$ is reduced, then so is $\mathcal{O}_{S, s}^ h$, but this is not true for the completion in general. Insert future references here. </p>
</article>